{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Getting the Client", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Partnership Accepted", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Changing Topics ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " In English, sometimes we need to interrupt people. This can be because we need to say something, express our opinion, or make a suggestion. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In a conversation, changing the topic is acceptable and perfectly normal. Once the other person has stopped speaking, you will need to return to the topic you were previously talking about.  <br /><br /> Here are some common ways you can do this: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">   Changing the topic   </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul> \\t<li> Speaking of \u2026  </li> \\t<li> By the way \u2026  </li> \\t<li> On that note \u2026 </li> \\t<li> Oh, that reminds me \u2026 </li> \\t<li> But \u2026  </li>  </ul>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "\"We should have a party to celebrate the new contract.\"", "type": "example"}, {"content": "\"Absolutely. <span class=\"underline\">Speaking of</span> parties, we need to find a good caterer.\" ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Giving and Exchanging Opinions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Conversations are far more interesting when people interact during the conversation. It is important to ask for others' opinions on a subject as well as giving your own.  <br /><br /> Here are some ways you can ask for and give opinions: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">    Asking for Opinions     </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">    Giving Opinions     </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\">Always ask questions that encourage a response:</span>  <ul> \\t<li>What do you think about \u2026 ?</li> \\t<li>What do you think of \u2026 ?</li> \\t<li>How do you feel (about \u2026 )? </li> \\t<li>Should I \u2026 ?</li> \\t<li>How do you want to \u2026 ?</li> \\t<li>How about you?</li> \\t</ul> \\t <span class=\\\"underline\\\">\\tUse tag questions</span><br />  <span class=\\\"underline\\\">1. positive verb + negative tag</span><br /> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \\\"yes\\\".<br /> <ul> \\t<li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">You <span class=\\\"strong\\\">were</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\\\"strong\\\">weren't you</span>? </li></span> \\t</ul> <span class=\\\"underline\\\">2. negative verb + positive tag </span><br /> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \\\"no\\\". <br /> <ul> \\t<li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">You <span class=\\\"strong\\\">weren't </span>taken by surprise, <span class=\\\"strong\\\">were you</span>? </li> \\t</ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\">When you give opinions, make your opinions less forceful by using neutral statements:</span>  <ul> \\t<li>I could \u2026 (+ verb) </li> \\t<li>This/That was \u2026 (+ adjective + noun)</li> \\t<li>I think \u2026 (+ clause) </li> \\t<li>I must say I \u2026 (+ verb phrase)</li> \\t<li>To be honest \u2026 (+ clause)</li> \\t<li>(clause) \u2026 if you ask me. </li> \\t<li>I could be wrong, but \u2026 (+ clause) </li> \\t<li>I felt that \u2026 (+ clause) </li> \\t</ul>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Jay</span>: \"I'm happy we got the contract.\"<br><span class=\"strong\">Mary</span>: \"You <span class=\"strong\">were</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">weren't you</span>?\"<br><span class=\"strong\">Jay</span>: \"<span class=\"strong\">I must say</span> that I was. <span class=\"strong\">I thought </span>they would offer the contract to our competitor.\"", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "luncheon ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a formal lunch", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We should plan a luncheon for when Peter gets back.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when planning the food needed for a party.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "caterer ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person or company whose job is to provide food and drinks at a business meeting or special occasion ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Should I look into hiring a caterer? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "vegan ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who does not eat any animal products such as meat, milk or eggs", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are some vegans in the company.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "vegetarian ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "eating no meat or fish", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm vegetarian and don't eat meat. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gluten-free ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "eating no foods that contain a sticky substance which is found in wheat flour", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm on a gluten-free diet.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "high protein ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " eating foods that contain substances your body needs in order to grow and remain strong ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I think she's on a high protein diet so we need to.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "low-sodium ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "eating foods that contain a small amount of salt", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm on a low-sodium diet.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "low-fat ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "eating foods that contain a small amount of oily substances", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: How do you feel about following a low-fat diet?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob01aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Plan a small office party to celebrate a new achievement. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose t